// neon.js — NÉON, a minimalist brick breaker (zero dependencies).
//
// This file mixes game logic and rendering in a few places (see ISSUES.md #2):
// brick collision resolution lives in `step()` behind `bounceBricks()` (moved
// out of the draw loop when fixing #1), and `frame()` still scans every brick
// on every frame. This is deliberate debt, ripe for a refactor.
//
// The module runs nothing on import: only `boot()` touches the DOM. Pure
// logic can therefore be imported from the tests (`node --test`) without a
// browser.

